The CRD API module under api/ is licensed under the Apache License, Version
2.0 (Apache-2.0). See api/LICENSE, or LICENSE-Apache-SDK at the root, for the
full license text.

This split is intentional and load-bearing. The api/ module carries only the
Go types for Keystone's custom resources, and anything that talks to Keystone
must import them: the client SDKs, third-party providers (Crossplane,
Terraform, and so on), and any controller that reads or writes these
resources. Licensing api/ permissively is what lets those integrate without
inheriting AGPL. Licensing it under AGPL would defeat the split entirely,
because a permissively-licensed consumer that links an AGPL module produces a
combined work under AGPL terms.

